# EXPECT: which the importing program also uses
#
# Splicing a module's top level into the program's scope is only equivalent to
# the VM's separate module env while the names are DISJOINT. Here the program
# binds `counter` INSIDE A FUNCTION BODY — invisible to the first version of
# the guard, which walked top-level statements only, so the module's private
# state was silently overwritten: VM 0/1, AOT 999/1000, build rc=0, empty log.
import _mod_priv
define reset() as:
    counter is 999
    return 0
x is reset of null
print of (_mod_priv.bump of null)
